1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,791
Meet Claro, banking support in Spanish and Portuguese.

2
00:00:03,791 --> 00:00:09,745
This is a working historical sandbox with team authored fixtures, not a
connection to real bank accounts.

3
00:00:09,745 --> 00:00:16,632
We complete one workflow: understand a transaction, report an unrecognized
charge, and hand off with evidence.

4
00:00:17,532 --> 00:00:21,146
Here, the Portuguese customer asks whether a payment went through.

5
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:24,197
Claro asks which transaction, instead of guessing.

6
00:00:24,197 --> 00:00:31,090
After a selection, it reports thirty eight dollars and fifty cents as pending,
preserving the currency and historical date.

7
00:00:31,090 --> 00:00:35,024
The answer comes from an authorized record tool, with source references.

8
00:00:35,924 --> 00:00:38,793
The customer says they do not recognize this charge.

9
00:00:38,793 --> 00:00:43,144
Claro prepares a human review case, but nothing has been created yet.

10
00:00:43,144 --> 00:00:46,195
Intent classification helps understand the request.

11
00:00:46,195 --> 00:00:51,924
Deterministic service rules control permissions, required context, and which
actions are allowed.

12
00:00:52,824 --> 00:00:56,850
A separate confirmation dialog names the sandbox action and its limits.

13
00:00:56,850 --> 00:01:01,796
The service requires the valid session, the correct role, and a CSRF token.

14
00:01:01,796 --> 00:01:05,395
Typing yes in the conversation cannot execute the case creation.

15
00:01:06,295 --> 00:01:09,384
The confirmed case is now saved and read back from storage.

16
00:01:09,384 --> 00:01:12,338
Only then does Claro show this verified reference.

17
00:01:12,338 --> 00:01:17,744
Retries reuse an idempotency key, so a dropped response does not create
another case.

18
00:01:17,744 --> 00:01:21,699
A verification failure produces an error, never a success claim.

19
00:01:22,599 --> 00:01:30,572
In the same isolated workspace, an analyst receives the allegation,
transaction facts, evidence, and open questions.

20
00:01:30,572 --> 00:01:35,827
Risk is unavailable for these out of domain fixtures, rather than shown as a
misleading zero.

21
00:01:35,827 --> 00:01:39,158
The analyst can close the review or request more information.

22
00:01:39,158 --> 00:01:41,602
Neither outcome grants a refund or proves fraud.

23
00:01:42,502 --> 00:01:49,815
The application uses one FastAPI service, a local language classifier, and a
transactional sandbox case store.

24
00:01:49,815 --> 00:01:54,183
Offline data preparation and model evaluation stay outside requests.

25
00:01:54,183 --> 00:01:57,527
The browser shows actual workspace activity and latency.

26
00:01:57,527 --> 00:02:01,517
Zero model API spend does not mean zero infrastructure cost.

27
00:02:02,417 --> 00:02:10,384
We compare rules, a trained TF-IDF classifier, and local Gemma on the same one
hundred forty authored bilingual scenarios.

28
00:02:10,384 --> 00:02:15,214
The selected classifier reaches an intent macro F one of eighty two point
three percent.

29
00:02:15,214 --> 00:02:19,185
The complete workflow has a separate evaluation with failures disclosed.

30
00:02:19,185 --> 00:02:23,839
These tests have no independent human review and cannot establish production
accuracy.

31
00:02:24,739 --> 00:02:30,567
The fraud experiment is equally explicit: its candidates did not pass the
validation promotion gate.

32
00:02:30,567 --> 00:02:34,622
We retain the baseline and never let a low score dismiss a customer's report.

33
00:02:34,622 --> 00:02:43,931
Claro delivers a working bilingual workflow, traceable evidence, and a human
handoff, with honest boundaries for what remains before real banking
production.
